    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Canadian open data API documentation - CanQuery" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Build with Canadian public data: working curl, Python and JavaScript examples, endpoint reference, API keys, pagination, preparation and error handling." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://canquery.com/og-image.svg" />
    <!-- seo:end --><meta name="canquery-analytics-site" content="01a02c60-cd0a-77f4-8680-7e9e317534a1" /><link rel="modulepreload" crossorigin href="/assets/DocsPage-abc123.js" />
<link rel="stylesheet" crossorigin href="/assets/DocsPage-abc123.css" />
<link rel="modulepreload" crossorigin href="/assets/shared-abc123.js" />
</head><body><div id="root"><main class="cq-seo-snapshot max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-8" data-cq-seo-snapshot="true"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">CanQuery</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">CanQuery API documentation</span></li></ol></nav><article><h1>CanQuery API documentation</h1><p>Build your first Canadian public-data integration with working examples, resource capabilities, typed endpoint reference and practical guidance for limits, pagination and retries.</p><p><a href="/pricing">Plans &amp; credits</a></p><nav aria-label="Documentation sections"><a href="#quickstart">First request</a> · <a href="#workflow">Toronto workflow</a> · <a href="#preparation-example">Preparation example</a> · <a href="#capabilities">Resource capabilities</a> · <a href="#reference">Endpoint reference</a> · <a href="#reliability">Reliable integrations</a></nav><section id="quickstart"><h2>Your first API request</h2><ol><li><a href="/signup">Create and verify a Free account</a>.</li><li><a href="/account">Create an API key</a> and save it in the CANQUERY_API_KEY environment variable on your server. Never expose it in a website or public repository.</li><li>Read metadata before querying rows:</li></ol><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Request example"><code>curl &quot;https://canquery.com/api/v1/resources/ckan-toronto-open-data-resource-6d0229af-bc54-46de-9c2b-26759b01dd05&quot; \\
  -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer $CANQUERY_API_KEY&quot;</code></pre><p>JSON successes normally contain data, pagination.nextCursor and meta. CSV exports, vector tiles, empty responses and /healthz have separate formats. Use an API key for new integrations. Anonymous compatibility is currently available.</p></section><section id="workflow"><h2>A reporting workflow you can reuse</h2><p>Discover a dataset, choose a resource, inspect its query_mode and preparation metadata, then filter the recorded fields. This example selects STREET_NAME equal to KING in Toronto’s active-permits resource.</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Request example"><code>curl --get &quot;https://canquery.com/api/v1/resources/ckan-toronto-open-data-resource-6d0229af-bc54-46de-9c2b-26759b01dd05/query&quot; \\
  -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer $CANQUERY_API_KEY&quot; \\
  --data-urlencode &#39;filters={&quot;STREET_NAME&quot;:&quot;KING&quot;}&#39; \\
  --data-urlencode &#39;limit=5&#39;</code></pre><p>For a bounded CSV, use the same filters with /query.csv. Export starts at offset zero and includes at most 10,000 rows. Keep provenance, publisher licence and retrieval time with your report. The dataset contains active applications and permits, not a complete history.</p><p><a href="/datasets/toronto-open-data-building-permits-active-permits">Toronto active building permits: source and context</a> · <a href="/blog/toronto-building-permits">Guide: active versus cleared permits and street filters</a></p></section><section id="preparation-example"><h2>Prepare a public file for a research extract</h2><p>Use ECCC CABIN Yukon River resource <code>718489a5-d132-4ee9-ab6f-0e2644297b78</code>. The selected CSV is not available through the federal DataStore. CanQuery decodes the UTF-16 download, imports and hosts a table, and supports bounded requests. ECCC also provides separate CABIN tools; this is not a claim that the publisher has no other interfaces.</p><p><a href="https://open.canada.ca/data/en/dataset/13564ca4-e330-40a5-9521-bfb1be767147">Publisher catalogue and Open Government Licence–Canada</a> · <a href="https://cabin-rcba.ec.gc.ca/Cabin/opendata/cabin_benthic_data_mda09_1987-present.csv">Original CSV</a> · <a href="https://www.canada.ca/en/environment-climate-change/services/canadian-aquatic-biomonitoring-network/database.html">Publisher database tools</a></p><ol><li>GET resource metadata. If a current prepared table exists, continue to the query.</li><li>For an eligible unprepared or stale resource, POST /prepare.</li><li>For a 202 response, poll its job serially at least three seconds apart, honour Retry-After and stop at done or failed. Stop locally after ten minutes and retain the job ID; this does not fail or cancel shared work.</li><li>Re-read metadata for the schema, freshness and preparation timestamp.</li><li>GET /query with <code>filters={&quot;Year/Année&quot;:2024,&quot;Family/Famille&quot;:&quot;Chironomidae&quot;}</code>, <code>sort=_id asc</code> and <code>limit=10</code>.</li></ol><p>The example counts matching records, not individual organisms or water quality. You still interpret taxonomy, coverage and publisher-specific values. Preserve publisher modification, preparation and retrieval dates as separate events. Enable JavaScript for runnable curl, Python and Node.js recipes and the verified result excerpt.</p><table><caption>Credits for the requests shown, using an existing API key</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Workflow</th><th scope="col">Credits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Inspect a ready resource, then query rows</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Inspect, admit a new preparation, poll, inspect the prepared schema, query rows</th><td>103</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Later inspect and query while the copy remains ready</th><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Polling costs zero. Joining existing work reduces the complete preparation sequence to 3 credits. A direct repeat query costs 1; an optional CSV export adds 25. An aggregate instead of the cold sequence’s row query totals 112. Discovery and other additional successful requests use their own credits.</p></section><section id="capabilities"><h2>Check what a resource supports</h2><ul><li>datastore: live upstream rows and equality filters; no aggregation.</li><li>ingested: prepared local rows, recorded-column filters, aggregation and whole-file profiles.</li><li>ingestable: eligible file; explicitly request /prepare, poll the returned job, then re-read metadata.</li><li>file-only: use the original download. Map capability is separate.</li></ul><p>Preparation can return 200 for a current copy or 202 with shared work. Limits and publisher availability apply. /ingest remains a legacy compatibility endpoint and does not refresh a ready copy.</p></section><section id="reference"><h2>Endpoint reference</h2><p><a href="/api/v1/openapi.json">Download OpenAPI 3.1: typed parameters, response schemas and examples</a>. Enable JavaScript for searchable parameters and code examples.</p><p><a href="/blog/uxbridge-ward-boundaries-map">Map example: Uxbridge ward boundaries and GIS downloads</a></p><details id="listDatasets"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/datasets</code> — Search datasets</summary><p>Discover admitted catalogue records. Availability of metadata does not guarantee a working file, table or map. Catalogue reads never request preparation. Follow pagination.nextCursor until null.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>q</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Catalogue search text, trimmed; at most 200 characters.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>org</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Publisher name or identity.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>format</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Recorded resource format.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>keyword</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Recorded dataset keyword.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>place</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Canonical place ID or slug; includes configured inherited coverage.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>source</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Catalogue source ID.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>mappable</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Only datasets with maps. Use true or 1; omit to disable. false is invalid.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>limit</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Page size; values above 100 are clamped to 100.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>cursor</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Nonnegative offset. Pass pagination.nextCursor unchanged; omit for the first page.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getDataset"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/datasets/{idOrName}</code> — Get a dataset</summary><p>Resolve a canonical dataset ID or published name/slug. Includes resources, capabilities and source-specific licence/provenance.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>idOrName</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Canonical dataset ID or published name/slug.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="listOrganizations"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/organizations</code> — List publishers</summary><p>Literal bilingual publisher search with optional source/place scope. Uses catalogue pagination.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>q</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Literal bilingual publisher search.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>source</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Catalogue source ID.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>place</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Canonical place ID or slug; includes configured inherited coverage.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>limit</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Page size; values above 100 are clamped to 100.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>cursor</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Nonnegative offset. Pass pagination.nextCursor unchanged; omit for the first page.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getOrganization"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/organizations/{name}</code> — Get a publisher</summary><p>Publisher identity, catalogue and capability counts, and place context.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>name</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Publisher name or identity, at most 200 characters.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="listPlaces"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/places</code> — List places</summary><p>Search canonical geographical identities and their direct/inherited coverage. Uses catalogue pagination.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>q</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Catalogue search text, trimmed; at most 200 characters.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>kind</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Place type.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>parent</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Canonical parent ID or slug.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>featured</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Use true or 1 for featured places; omit to disable.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>limit</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Page size; values above 100 are clamped to 100.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>cursor</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Nonnegative offset. Pass pagination.nextCursor unchanged; omit for the first page.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getPlace"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/places/{idOrSlug}</code> — Get a place</summary><p>Resolve a canonical ID, slug or durable alias. Includes ancestry, children, viewport and coverage. API lookup does not redirect like an HTML alias.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>idOrSlug</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Canonical place ID, slug or historical alias.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="listSources"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/sources</code> — List catalogue sources</summary><p>Persisted publisher portals, provenance hosts, catalogue counts and last successful sync. This endpoint is not paginated.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>place</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Canonical place ID or slug; includes configured inherited coverage.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getResource"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/resources/{id}</code> — Inspect resource capabilities</summary><p>Read query_mode, preparation, ingestion, map and provenance before querying. A map can exist on a file-only table resource. Metadata reads neither prepare files nor renew local-copy activity. Preparation time differs from publisher modification time; source changes can remain undiscovered when publisher version metadata is unchanged.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Resource ID from dataset or resource metadata.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="listRecentlyPrepared"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/resources/recently-unlocked</code> — List recently prepared resources</summary><p>Recent ready local copies. The historical route name is retained. Reading the list does not prepare files.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>place</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Canonical place ID or slug; includes configured inherited coverage.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>limit</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Page size; values above 20 are clamped to 20.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="listPopularResources"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/resources/popular</code> — List popular resources</summary><p>Counts CanQuery query-log hits, not publisher downloads.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>place</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Canonical place ID or slug; includes configured inherited coverage.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>days</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Lookback days; values above 30 are clamped.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>limit</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Page size; values above 20 are clamped to 20.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="queryResource"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/resources/{id}/query</code> — Query rows or aggregate</summary><p>Ready local snapshots take precedence over live CKAN DataStore. Live DataStore supports equality filters only, with no aggregation. Local aggregates cover the complete filtered snapshot; total then counts groups, not rows. Local reads renew copy activity and successful queries record popularity. Local responses include meta.snapshot, retrieval time and deployment limits. Supply snapshot on subsequent pages to require identical stored rows and schema; 409 requires an explicit new extraction. Catalogue provenance and publisher modification timestamps are observed at retrieval, not frozen at preparation. source_metadata_version is not a downloaded-content checksum. A 409 never automatically enqueues preparation; inspect metadata and explicitly use /prepare when supported. Aggregations have an additional 30 requests/minute limit and consume expensive-request concurrency.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Resource ID from dataset or resource metadata.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>snapshot</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Require this exact local snapshot. A replaced or unavailable copy returns 409 SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE; no automatic fallback or preparation. This token does not promise retention or source-content freshness.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>q</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Search within resource rows (not catalogue search); at most 200 characters. Local search uses case-insensitive ILIKE patterns.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>filters</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>URL-encoded JSON object, at most 2,000 characters and 20 column keys of 1–63 characters. Exact recorded field names; conditions combine with AND. Scalars mean equality. Objects use op and value: eq, lt, gt, lte, gte, contains. Live DataStore supports eq only. eq:null means IS NULL locally; contains preserves % and _ SQL wildcard meanings.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>sort</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Exact field name, optionally followed by asc or desc. Local row sorting also accepts _id; aggregates accept key or value. An exact field name wins over a direction suffix. Live DataStore values are limited to 100 characters.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>group_by</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Prepared tables only: exact recorded grouping field. Required together with agg.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>agg</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Prepared tables only. count forbids agg_column; other functions require it. sum/avg require a numeric field.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>agg_column</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Recorded measure field for sum, avg, min or max; forbidden with count.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>bucket</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Optional temporal grouping; group_by must be DATE or TIMESTAMPTZ.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>limit</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Page size; values above 100 are clamped to 100.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>offset</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Row/group offset; independent of catalogue cursor. Avoid relying on a stable snapshot across page calls.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="exportResourceCsv"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/resources/{id}/query.csv</code> — Export a bounded CSV</summary><p>Exports from offset zero, at most 10000 rows (deployment cap; hard maximum 10,000). Same query capabilities as /query, including local full-snapshot aggregation before limiting groups. There is no CSV pagination or full-file guarantee. Use the original download for complete publisher files. Formula-like spreadsheet cells are neutralized. A failure after headers closes the partial response: discard incomplete output and retry within limits. Keyed failed/interrupted exports are refunded. Ten exports/minute plus plan request/concurrency limits.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Resource ID from dataset or resource metadata.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>snapshot</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Require this exact local snapshot. A replaced or unavailable copy returns 409 SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE; no automatic fallback or preparation. This token does not promise retention or source-content freshness.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>q</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Search within resource rows (not catalogue search); at most 200 characters. Local search uses case-insensitive ILIKE patterns.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>filters</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>URL-encoded JSON object, at most 2,000 characters and 20 column keys of 1–63 characters. Exact recorded field names; conditions combine with AND. Scalars mean equality. Objects use op and value: eq, lt, gt, lte, gte, contains. Live DataStore supports eq only. eq:null means IS NULL locally; contains preserves % and _ SQL wildcard meanings.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>sort</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Exact field name, optionally followed by asc or desc. Local row sorting also accepts _id; aggregates accept key or value. An exact field name wins over a direction suffix. Live DataStore values are limited to 100 characters.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>group_by</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Prepared tables only: exact recorded grouping field. Required together with agg.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>agg</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Prepared tables only. count forbids agg_column; other functions require it. sum/avg require a numeric field.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>agg_column</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Recorded measure field for sum, avg, min or max; forbidden with count.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>bucket</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Optional temporal grouping; group_by must be DATE or TIMESTAMPTZ.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="profileResource"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/resources/{id}/profile</code> — Profile a prepared table</summary><p>Requires a ready local snapshot. Describes the whole file, not current filters. At most the first 60 recorded non-_id fields; numeric fields add min/max/avg and date fields min/max. Successful reads renew activity. Twenty requests/minute plus plan request/concurrency limits.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Resource ID from dataset or resource metadata.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>snapshot</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Require this exact local snapshot. A replaced or unavailable copy returns 409 SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE; no automatic fallback or preparation. This token does not promise retention or source-content freshness.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="prepareResource"><summary><code>POST /api/v1/resources/{id}/prepare</code> — Prepare or refresh a file</summary><p>No body. Returns 200 for a current copy or 202 for a new/shared job. Only a newly admitted job deducts preparation credits. A terminal failure without a result published by that job returns the actual debit to its original allowance period exactly once. Retries retain the charge; stopping polling does not fail the job. A failed refresh returns its own charge even if an older copy still serves. A successful empty table counts as success; later expiry or eviction does not return credits. This is an account-credit reversal, not a payment refund. Current copies, joins and polling cost zero but still count toward request limits. Keyed new jobs are capped at 20/account/hour; anonymous admission has a configured per-IP limit. A shared active-queue ceiling and format/size/row/column/storage caps also apply. A stale copy can continue serving during refresh. Paused admission returns 429 even for current copies. Anonymous requests from self-identified crawlers can read current copies and join shared jobs but cannot start new ones (429 AUTOMATED_CLIENT). Honour cooldown Retry-After; a new source version can bypass the old cooldown. No scheduled-refresh guarantee.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Resource ID from dataset or resource metadata.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="ingestResourceLegacy"><summary><code>POST /api/v1/resources/{id}/ingest</code> — Prepare a file (legacy)</summary><p>No body. Compatibility endpoint; new integrations should use /prepare for freshness and refresh. It returns an existing ready copy without refreshing stale data. Five requests/hour, plus shared limits. New-job charging matches /prepare.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Resource ID from dataset or resource metadata.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="renewResourceActivity"><summary><code>POST /api/v1/resources/{id}/activity</code> — Renew local-copy activity</summary><p>No body. Renews an existing ready copy without preparing a file or recording popularity. A 409 means the copy is unavailable or replaced; re-read metadata. Zero credits still counts toward request limits.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Resource ID from dataset or resource metadata.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getPreparationJob"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/jobs/{id}</code> — Poll a preparation job</summary><p>Poll one request at a time with a bounded delay and honour Retry-After on errors. A done job is historical: re-read resource metadata before querying because a prepared copy may expire. Failure messages are sanitized; failure_reason and retry_at explain retry eligibility. Zero credits still counts toward request limits.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>integer</td><td>Yes</td><td>Positive job ID returned by preparation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getMapViewport"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/resources/{id}/map</code> — Get a bounded map viewport</summary><p>Enveloped WGS84 GeoJSON for admitted ArcGIS, local PostGIS or PMTiles maps. live=true identifies the viewport interface; it does not promise a publisher fetch on every call. Check returned/truncated; requests are capped at 1,000 features and 8 MiB. PMTiles viewport decoding also bounds tile count. Sixty viewport calls/minute plus plan request/concurrency limits.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Resource ID from dataset or resource metadata.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>bbox</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Required WGS84 west,south,east,north: -180 ≤ west &lt; east ≤ 180 and -90 ≤ south &lt; north ≤ 90.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>zoom</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Integer zoom level.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>limit</code></th><td>query</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Feature ceiling; out-of-range values return 400.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getMapTile"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/resources/{id}/map/tiles/{version}/{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf</code> — Get a vector tile</summary><p>PMTiles maps only. Copy the current tiles template/version and zoom range from resource metadata. Coordinates must fit the tile grid and archive zoom range. Anonymous successful tiles cache immutably for one year; keyed responses remain private, no-store. Up to 240 tiles/minute, also subject to the keyed plan request limit.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>id</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Resource ID from dataset or resource metadata.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>version</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Current map version from resource metadata.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>z</code></th><td>path</td><td>integer</td><td>Yes</td><td>Zoom within this archive’s min_zoom/max_zoom (0–22).</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>x</code></th><td>path</td><td>integer</td><td>Yes</td><td>Tile coordinate from 0 through 2^z − 1.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>y</code></th><td>path</td><td>integer</td><td>Yes</td><td>Tile coordinate from 0 through 2^z − 1.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getCatalogueStats"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/stats</code> — Get catalogue statistics</summary><p>Briefly cached counts; capabilities overlap. These are dated observations, not guaranteed coverage or publisher availability.</p></details><details id="getTopDownloads"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/insights/top-downloads</code> — Get the publisher download leaderboard</summary><p>Publisher-reported download statistics with selected representatives. Distinct from CanQuery query popularity; meta.period identifies the reporting month.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>lang</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>French when fr; otherwise English.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getFeaturedPreviews"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/insights/featured</code> — Get prepared chart previews</summary><p>Up to 12 validated previews from already prepared Top 100 representatives. No preparation is admitted. Context gives aggregation, snapshot time, displayed/total groups and known missing metrics; this is neither a chart-rendering API nor a scheduled-refresh service.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>lang</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>French when fr; otherwise English.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="listGuides"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/blog</code> — List data guides</summary><p>Published guide summaries; reads bundled content without querying the catalogue.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>lang</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Guide language; must be en or fr.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>place</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Guide place slug.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>dataset</code></th><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Canonical dataset ID or published slug.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getGuide"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/blog/{lang}/{slug}</code> — Get a data guide</summary><p>Published guide edition including sanitized bodyHtml and translation links.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>lang</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Guide edition language.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><code>slug</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Published localized guide slug.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getRepositoryMetadata"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/repo</code> — Get repository metadata</summary><p>Cached public GitHub star count. data may be null when GitHub is unavailable.</p></details><details id="getOperations"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/ops</code> — Inspect job and map health</summary><p>Public and unmetered. HTTP 200 or 503 uses the same envelope according to data.ok. Preparation counters alone do not change ok; inspect queue age and worker state separately. Health does not guarantee every file is available.</p></details><details id="getHealth"><summary><code>GET /healthz</code> — Check database and federal upstream</summary><p>Site-root path /healthz (not /api/v1/healthz). Public, unmetered, unenveloped reachability check; not a worker or catalogue-wide availability check.</p></details><details id="getReadiness"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/readyz</code> — Check application and database availability</summary><p>Site-root path. Public, unmetered and no-store. Checks database connectivity without requiring an upstream publisher or worker to be healthy.</p></details><details id="getComponentHealth"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/ops/components/{component}</code> — Inspect one operational component</summary><p>Public, unmetered and no-store. Sanitized host observations older than 180 seconds fail closed with HTTP 503. Independent components separate availability, preparation, maps, sources, commercial backlogs, backups and storage. Existing /ops semantics remain unchanged.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" aria-label="Endpoint parameters"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><code>component</code></th><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Operational component to inspect.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details id="getOpenApi"><summary><code>GET /api/v1/openapi.json</code> — Download the OpenAPI contract</summary><p>Public, unmetered OpenAPI 3.1 document. Import into compatible developer tools. Examples are synthetic and do not establish current publisher data or availability.</p></details></section><section id="reliability"><h2>Operate reliably</h2><p>Catalogue lists use the returned nextCursor offset string until null. Row queries use limit/offset and data.total; separate requests do not guarantee one unchanged snapshot. Local filters use exact recorded columns and combine with AND. CSV exports are capped; discard partial output after a failed stream.</p><p>Account keys share credits, request rates and expensive-request concurrency. X-CanQuery-Credits-Remaining includes pending reservations. Successful cached requests count. Successful cached requests count. Failed ordinary requests and interrupted exports return their credits. A new preparation deducts 100 credits; a terminal failure without a result published by that job returns its actual debit once to the original allowance period. Retries retain the debit. A client timeout does not fail or cancel the shared job. A failed refresh returns its charge even if an older table remains usable. Valid empty tables count as success; later expiry or eviction does not return credits. This is an account-credit adjustment, not a cash refund. Joining jobs and polling cost zero credits but still count toward request limits.</p><p>Distinguish QUOTA_EXCEEDED from RATE_LIMIT, CONCURRENCY_LIMIT, PREPARATION_BUSY, PREPARATION_COOLDOWN and AUTOMATED_CLIENT. Honour Retry-After and bound retries; do not repeatedly retry exhausted allowances, authentication errors or unsupported files. Include X-Request-Id when contacting support.</p><p>Publisher modification time, preparation time and retrieval time differ. Copies may expire, upstream files may change, and there is no scheduled-refresh guarantee.</p></section><section><h2>Explore CanQuery</h2><ul><li><a href="/">Search the catalogue</a></li></ul></section></article></main></div></body></html>",
    "cacheControl": "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate",
    "location": null,
    "status": 200,
  },
  "/faq": {
    "body": "<!doctype html><html><head><!-- seo:start -->
    <title>Frequently asked questions - CanQuery</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Get answers about Canadian open data, supported tables and maps, file preparation, developer accounts and contacting CanQuery support." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://canquery.com/faq" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Frequently asked questions - CanQuery" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Get answers about Canadian open data, supported tables and maps, file preparation, developer accounts and contacting CanQuery support." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://canquery.com/faq" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="CanQuery" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://canquery.com/og-image.svg" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Frequently asked questions - CanQuery" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Get answers about Canadian open data, supported tables and maps, file preparation, developer accounts and contacting CanQuery support." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://canquery.com/og-image.svg" />
    <!-- seo:end --><meta name="canquery-analytics-site" content="01a02c60-cd0a-77f4-8680-7e9e317534a1" /><link rel="modulepreload" crossorigin href="/assets/FaqPage-abc123.js" />
<link rel="stylesheet" crossorigin href="/assets/FaqPage-abc123.css" />
<link rel="modulepreload" crossorigin href="/assets/shared-abc123.js" />
</head><body><div id="root"><main class="cq-seo-snapshot max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-8" data-cq-seo-snapshot="true"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">CanQuery</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">Frequently asked questions</span></li></ol></nav><article><h1>Frequently asked questions</h1><p>A few useful answers about finding data, preparing tables and using your developer account.</p><section id="getting-started"><h2>Getting started</h2><details><summary>What can I do with CanQuery?</summary><p>Search Canadian public-data catalogues by topic, place, publisher or format. Follow original downloads, explore supported tables and maps, or use the developer API in your own tools. A catalogue listing does not guarantee that every file is available or can be queried.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need an account?</summary><p>You can browse the website and use its supported data tools without an account. A verified developer account lets you create API keys and view your API usage. Creating a Free account does not start a paid subscription.</p></details><details><summary>Where does the data come from, and can I reuse it?</summary><p>The data comes from public-sector publishers, including federal, municipal, regional and territorial sources. Dataset pages link to the publisher, source portal and applicable licence. Check that licence and its attribution requirements before reusing the data; different datasets can have different terms.</p></details></section><section id="working-with-data"><h2>Working with data</h2><details><summary>Why do some resources only offer a download?</summary><p>Table and map support depend on the resource. Supported live tables can be queried directly, while eligible CSV and Excel files can be prepared for querying. Other formats, oversized files or unavailable publisher downloads may remain download-only. A resource can support a map without supporting a table.</p></details><details><summary>What happens when a file is being prepared?</summary><p>When you open an eligible resource in Table or Chart, CanQuery may download the file and prepare a queryable copy. Visitors share existing preparation work. File, row, column and storage limits apply. Opening catalogue pages or Map does not start table preparation.</p></details><details><summary>How fresh is a prepared table?</summary><p>A prepared table is a snapshot, not a continuously updated feed. CanQuery can refresh an eligible copy on a later visit when tracked source metadata changes. Publisher modification and preparation times are different. Copies may expire after inactivity or be evicted, so check the displayed dates and original source before relying on the data.</p></details><details><summary>Can I download the complete dataset?</summary><p>Use the original publisher download when you need the source file. CanQuery CSV exports are bounded to at most 10,000 rows and can be subject to a lower installed limit. Filters and aggregation affect the export. An export is not a guarantee of a complete historical dataset.</p></details></section><section id="accounts-and-api"><h2>Accounts and the API</h2><details><summary>What is the difference between Free and Business?</summary><p>Both plans offer the same supported data capabilities. Business provides a larger API allowance, more keys and higher request capacity. It does not remove file, query, export or map limits. See Pricing for current prices and allowances.</p></details><details><summary>How do API credits work?</summary><p>Keyed API requests use credits according to the operation. Successful cached requests still count. A newly admitted preparation job has its own charge; joining existing work, checking job status and renewing activity cost no credits. Rate and capacity limits still apply. The Pricing and API documentation pages explain current costs and workflow examples.</p></details><details><summary>Are credits returned if preparation fails?</summary><p>If a charged preparation job ends in failure without publishing a successful copy, its original charge is returned once to the original payer and allowance period. Internal retries or stopping polling do not establish failure. A return to an expired period does not add credits to the current period. These are account credits, not cash refunds.</p></details><details><summary>How do I cancel Business or get account help?</summary><p>Open the billing portal from your account to cancel before renewal. Access continues through the paid period, then follows Free allowances. Email support for billing questions, account deletion or help with verification and password-reset messages.</p></details></section><section id="support"><h2>Contact support</h2><p>Have a question, found a bug or need account help? Email us at: <a href="mailto:support@canquery.com">support@canquery.com</a></p><p>For a technical issue, include the page or resource URL, what you were trying to do and the error message. If available, include the time, HTTP status and X-Request-Id. Leave out API keys, passwords and sensitive query contents.</p><p>For the first few customers, the founder can help by email with one existing supported resource and one working query. Custom integrations need a separate scope.</p></section><section><h2>Explore CanQuery</h2><ul><li><a href="/docs">Read the API documentation</a></li><li><a href="/pricing">Compare plans and credits</a></li><li><a href="/terms">Read the service terms</a></li><li><a href="/privacy">Privacy and your data</a></li></ul></section></article></main></div></body></html>",
